    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40329" root="نقب" body-key="n">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَقِبٌ</span></b> , and, as a fem. epithet, ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَقْبَاءُ</span></b> , A camel
<i>whose feet have become worn in holes,</i> [or <i>worn
thin,</i>] <i>by walking.</i> (TA.) See the verb. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
The former may also signify <i>Having the scab,</i> or
<i>what first appears thereof.</i> (TA.) See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نُقْبٌ</span>.

